# Stage 4 owns its data and output rules, like the other three stages; the root
# .gitignore only keeps tool and OS noise out at any depth.
#
# The config rule is this repo's, not dotin's stage-4 scaffold's: the tracked file
# is the password-free `config/capstone.example.toml`, and only the local copy is
# ignored. A blanket `config/*.toml` ignore would leave a fresh clone with nothing
# to run the one-command chain from.

# Virtual environments
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# Python junk
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.env

# Jupyter writes these beside an open notebook. With two required notebooks a
# stray checkpoint copy in Git would read like an older delivery of one of them.
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*checkpoint.ipynb

# Raw inputs: the 9 Olist CSVs and any fresh-order file handed to the prediction
# entrypoint. Data, not deliverable.
data/raw/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep

# Rejected rows from the prediction entrypoint quote order values verbatim; a
# quarantine file in history would undo the "no raw data in Git" rule.
data/quarantine/*
!data/quarantine/.gitkeep

# Feature frames and the run manifest are regenerated by the chain from the
# database. Measured timings are copied into docs/evidence/ and committed there,
# so the manifest itself staying untracked costs nothing.
data/curated/*
!data/curated/.gitkeep
data/run_manifest*.json

# Raw terminal logs of a local run (machine paths, user names, host). They stay on
# the author's disk; only the measured numbers go into docs/PHASE0_REPORT.md or a
# committed evidence file. Evidence files already tracked (the red/green runs and
# phase0-baseline.txt) are not affected: .gitignore does not untrack files.
docs/evidence/*-real-run*.txt
# ... with one exception, and it is the reason the rule is stated as a rule: the student's own run of
# docs/evidence/frame-performance-run.py is the witness that closes checklist 5.3, and a checklist row
# quoting a file that git will not carry is a claim nobody downstream can check. The transcription
# `frame-performance-student-run.txt` is tracked either way; this line only lets the raw capture join
# it, on `git add docs/evidence/frame-performance-real-run.txt`. Nothing in the patch assumes it happened.
!docs/evidence/frame-performance-real-run.txt
docs/evidence/*.log

# Fitted models are outputs, not source
*.joblib

# Machine-specific config (paths, DB host). config/capstone.example.toml is the
# tracked contract; the password is never in either file.
config/capstone.toml
# a harness that died mid-run must not leave a decided config for the next `git add -A`
config/patch-0015-evidence.toml

# tool caches and OS junk
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.DS_Store
